-- title:
--   Finite-dimensionality of qⁿ-fixed vectors in the local span
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number, let $g$ be a cusp form of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(M)$, let $q$ be a prime, and let $\Phi : \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbf{A}_{\mathbf{Q}}) \to \mathbf{C}$ be a function on the adelic group $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of $\mathbf{Q}$ such that $g$ `IsAdelicLiftOf` $\Phi$, i.e. (i) $\Phi(\gamma x) = \Phi(x)$ for every $\gamma \in \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbf{Q})$ embedded diagonally and every adelic $x$, (ii) $\Phi(x u) = \Phi(x)$ for every $u$ in the group `finiteLevelOne` attached to the ideal $(M)$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbf{Q}}$, embedded from the finite adeles, and (iii) for every adelic $h$ whose finite component is trivial and whose real component $\mathrm{ratArchGL2}(h)$ has positive determinant, $\Phi(h)$ equals the value at $i$ of the weight-$2$ slash of $g$ by that real component. Let $n$ be a natural number. Then the following complex vector space is finite-dimensional: inside `AdelicSpan` $\Phi$, the span of all adelic translates $x \cdot \Phi$, the intersection of the submodule of vectors fixed by every element of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbf{Q}_q)$ all of whose entries of $h - 1$ and of $h^{-1} - 1$ have norm at most $q^{-n}$, with the span of the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbf{Q}_q)$-translates of the distinguished vector $\Phi$ itself.
--
--   This is the admissibility, in the form of finiteness of the spaces of vectors fixed by the congruence subgroups of level $q^n$, of the representation of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbf{Q}_q)$ generated by an adelic lift of a weight-two cusp form. It feeds the construction of a realisation of that local representation and, through it, the local analysis at $q$ used in the modularity arguments.
